+### Turning Wiki Reads Off
+
+To stop agents from reading the wiki, set this in `.ta/workflow.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[wiki]
+seed_context = false
+```
+
+The default is `true`, so projects without a `[wiki]` section behave as before. With `false`, the MCP gateway refuses `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types`, including calls from chat-mode sessions, and the background wiki sync stops filling the local cache. Each refusal names the setting, the file and how to turn reads back on. Writes are not affected: `ta_wiki_create`, `ta_wiki_update` and the draft-review path work as described above.
+
+`ta status` shows a `Wiki reads: OFF` line while the switch is off. A `seed_context` value that is not `true` or `false` is an error that names `.ta/workflow.toml` and the key; reads are refused until you fix it.
+
 ### Wiki Writes Are Reviewed
 
 `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` do not write to the wiki when an agent calls them. They check the input and queue the change in the goal's draft. Nothing reaches Wayfinder until you approve and apply that draft. `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` are unchanged and read live.
